{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfxsZXBkbgebFNMXkiBRV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four steps are done. The rule reads back as enabled.\n\n- **Data view:** the time field on 'Kibana Sample Data Logs' is `timestamp`. `response` is a string field, so I used `response.keyword` for the response-code panel and the rule.\n- **Dashboard:** 'S4-52a4ec68 Web logs' has two panels. One is a line chart of requests over time, and the other is a bar chart of requests by response code.\n- **Alert rule:** 'S4-52a4ec68 5xx errors' checks every minute. It fires when more than 10 requests have `response.keyword` from \"500\" to \"599\" within 5 minutes. The range is a string comparison, which covers every 5xx code because they are all three-digit strings. The rule was created disabled, so I enabled it.\n- **Panel edit:** the response-code panel is now titled 'Responses by code'. I didn't read the dashboard back afterwards to confirm the new title.\n- **Read-back:** the rule shows `enabled: true` and status `ok`.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":599,"cache_read_input_tokens":20758,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":599},"output_tokens":366,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0da1e72d-e9d9-58d9-b388-fca8d0eba393","uuid":"38332a37-f213-4c7c-9d07-aa85c97362bc","timestamp":"2026-10-12T19:11:11.296Z","request_id":"req_011CfxsZWt8rBCdqoqcy42Dh"}
